Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:07.100
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Disney posted the second episode of Rebels

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.790
early again on iTunes and the Disney XD website
and it brought back a couple of old friends.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.010
Also big heads up too, today at New York Comic
Con, they announced that they’d also be

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:25.780
airing a Guardians of The Galaxy animated
series on Disney XD next year.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.910
This will just be a video for rebels, but
I wanted to let you know about Guardians just

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:30.880
in case you didn’t see the news.

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.329
Careful for Rebels Spoilers if you haven’t
seen the episode.

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:34.520
It’s free right now on itunes.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.690
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go
Top 5 moments

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.980
Number 5 - The Star Tours Robot RX-24

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.329
Star Tours was a disneyland ride from 1987
to 2010.

00:00:44.329 --> 00:00:48.190
I hope you got a chance to ride it, but it
was like a virtual Star Wars adventure ride

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:51.239
that had a narrative and voice over work.

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:55.500
The droid that ushered you through everything
was RX-24, this guy right here.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:02.570
So his cameo is very similar to what he did
and said on the disneyland ride.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.720
The ship looks like the star tours ship too.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:08.689
But you may recognize the voice being done
by paul reubens, he’s the same guy that

00:01:08.689 --> 00:01:10.520
did the voice for the original ride.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:15.810
Here’s a little bit of the original audio
from the ride.

00:01:15.810 --> 00:01:31.999
It’s just awesome that they did this, it’s
a huge easter egg for anyone that got to go

00:01:31.999 --> 00:01:34.619
on the ride.

00:01:34.619 --> 00:01:39.499
Just for reference, disneyland replaced Star
Tours with an updated version of the ride

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.499
in 2011.

00:01:40.499 --> 00:01:43.340
They brought a bunch of original cast members
like Carrie Fisher to do voices for the new

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.340
ride and Paul Reubens to do this RX-24 guy
again.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:49.979
If any of you are Avatar Last Airbender or
Legend Of Korra fans, Dee Bradley Baker does

00:01:49.979 --> 00:01:51.979
the voice for Boba Fett.

00:01:51.979 --> 00:01:54.399
Number 4 - Zeb Backstory

00:01:54.399 --> 00:01:57.039
We learn a ton about Zeb’s history before
the events on the show.

00:01:57.039 --> 00:02:00.340
It’s a very similar story to what happened
to the Wookies on Kashyyyk.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:05.380
It turns out Agent Kallus ordered the use
of these special disruptor guns on the Lasat

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:10.270
people during a big final assault on his home
planet.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.890
It sounds like most of his people were killed.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:33.500
We also learn he was a member of the honor
guard because of his special bow rifle.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:37.470
Even though it looks like the staff weapons
used by general grievous’ droids in revenge

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.190
of the sith, the name bow rifle reminds me
of Chewbacca’s weapon, the bowcaster.

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:45.000
In case you didn’t see any of my other rebels
videos.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.020
Zeb’s race, the lasat is based on the original
ralph mcquarrie concept drawings for Wookies.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.470
So if you get chewbacca vibes from him.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:54.860
It’s intentional.

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:57.650
Number 3 - C3PO &amp; R2

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.420
It wouldn’t be Star Wars without a cameo
from these guys.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:03.890
Turns out they were secretly on a mission
for bail organa, so they haven’t passed

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:06.130
into the service of Princess Leia yet.

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:12.240
In george lucas’ original story materials
for episode 4, he describes her as being between

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.360
13 and 15, so I’d say right now where we
are on the show, she’s only about 11.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.360
In the expanded universe she became a senator
at 16, so the timeline is a little fuzzy.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.360
I’m not sure how long she had been a senator
when episode 4 picks up.

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:20.830
This isn’t their show though, so I understand
that they didn’t start the story with the

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:21.830
droids.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:26.490
In the original trilogy, George Lucas used
this old Akira Kurosawa technique to open

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:28.630
the movie with them.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:32.210
Kurosawa would just open samurai films from
the perspective of lesser characters and as

00:03:32.210 --> 00:03:38.090
you started to learn about the story from
them, they’d run into the main characters

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.670
and the perspective would shift.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:43.230
It would have been cool if they did that in
this episode.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.600
But I get why they chose not to.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:50.720
They did kind of end the episode on a moment
like this when Bail Organa referred to them

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.380
as a couple of rebels.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:57.990
Just making it seem like the crew of the ghost
were a small blip on the galaxy’s radar.

00:03:57.990 --> 00:04:00.260
Number 2 - Zeb vs kallus

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.209
This really did turn into a Zeb Episode, which
is great.

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.990
It just means more Steven Blum.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.400
We also found out that he and Kallus have
unkown history.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:12.750
Zeb was learning Kallus was behind the massacre
on his home planet.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:17.259
So what you’re seeing is the potential beginning
of a blood feud that will run across the rest

00:04:17.259 --> 00:04:18.909
of the season.

00:04:18.909 --> 00:04:24.620
Kallus was almost able to Kill Zeb this time,
so don’t be surprised if at some point Zeb

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:30.139
almost kills Kallus and it becomes an anakin
skywalker type situation where he has to decide

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:34.889
whether to kill him and go super dark or take
the high road and let him live, at the expense

00:04:34.889 --> 00:04:37.949
of any future evil shennanigans Kallus might
commit.

00:04:37.949 --> 00:04:57.680
There’s always that moral throughline in
star wars tv episodes, so if they chose the

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:01.219
right path in turning the guns over to Bail
Organa, then of course they won’t chose

00:05:01.219 --> 00:05:04.289
to kill anyone if given the chance.

00:05:04.289 --> 00:05:07.259
and my Number 1 moment - Bail Organa’s Ship

00:05:07.259 --> 00:05:10.699
You may have recognized him, but Phil Lamaar
came back to do the voice for Bail.

00:05:10.699 --> 00:05:12.130
He did the voice during Clone Wars.

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:25.439
In fact, so far, Rebels has used all the original
Clone Wars voice actors to do characters in

00:05:25.439 --> 00:05:27.189
the new series when they get cameos.

00:05:27.189 --> 00:05:28.189
Like Obi-Wan.

00:05:28.189 --> 00:05:31.819
It’s cute that Kanan leaves without knowing
who Bail Organa is, but the really interesting

00:05:31.819 --> 00:05:33.189
part was the last bit.

00:05:33.189 --> 00:05:35.819
Him referring to the Ghost as a band of Rebels.

00:05:35.819 --> 00:05:40.340
Disney was pretty clear that this tv series
would be kind of an origin story for the rebellion.

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.710
It’s not really about the rebellion though.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:44.020
It’s just about this small group of people.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:48.669
But the whole Spark of Rebellion first episode
implies that what they’ll be doing during

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:53.210
the tv series will inspire the people who
do form the rebellion.

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:55.820
Just as a brush up on your expanded universe
history.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:06:03.629
The official leaders of the Rebellion were
Bail Organa, Mon Mothma and Garm Bel Iblis.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:08.440
The listed date of formation, when the rebellion
officially became the rebel alliance was 2

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.360
years before episode 4.

00:06:10.360 --> 00:06:16.490
So it might go down in a future season of
rebels unless they mess with the timeline.

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:23.060
If we saw Bail Organa, there’s a good chance
we’ll see the other leaders.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:28.909
Let me know what your favorite moment was
and did you ever go on the old star tours

00:06:28.909 --> 00:06:32.199
ride or the new one?

00:06:32.199 --> 00:06:36.779
Overall I gave the episode a solid B plus
for amazing use of nostalgia.

00:06:36.779 --> 00:06:41.249
It’s very hard to create dramatic tension
when we already know what the endgame is,

00:06:41.249 --> 00:06:46.509
so the work is really unfolding these stories
in new an interesting ways.

00:06:46.509 --> 00:06:50.419
If you ever feel like the camera is lingering
on things for a long time, it’s probably

00:06:50.419 --> 00:06:52.659
because they laid in some easter eggs, which
is really what I spend a lot of my time during

00:06:52.659 --> 00:06:53.659
episodes doing.

00:06:53.659 --> 00:06:58.059
Playing the game where you see how many special
things you can spot.

00:06:58.059 --> 00:06:59.559
Like the landspeeder here.

00:06:59.559 --> 00:07:03.259
This is the same model that was inside Owen
and Beru Lars farm.

00:07:03.259 --> 00:07:07.750
You see it in episode 4 when luke starts cleaning
off 3PO and R2.

00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.550
It’s a different color, but you get the
idea.

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:11.629
Then there’s the Bow rifle and the bowcaster,
there’s probably a ton of stuff I missed.

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:16.839
So if you spotted any objects or references
just write them in the comments.

00:07:16.839 --> 00:07:20.969
The series is offically going to premiere
on Disney XD this monday, they’ll be airing

00:07:20.969 --> 00:07:22.229
